<title>SINGAPORE: Showpla buys remaining stake in unit.</title>
<headline>Showpla buys remaining stake in unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plastic mouldings company Showpla Asia Ltd said on Thursday it had bought the remaining 35 percent stake in its subsidiary Sanyo Showpla Manufacturing (SSM) for Singapore $2.541 million.</p>
<p>The stake was sold by Sanyo Industires (S) Pte Ltd and Sanyo Airconditioners (S) Pte Ltd, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The purchase will be paid for in cash. On completion of the deal, SSM will become Showpla's manufacturing arm.</p>
<p>SSM's name will be changed to Qian Hui Manufacturing (S) Pte Ltd, it said.</p>
<p>SSM manufactures large injection moulded plastic components.</p>
